---
/**
 * Daily Quote — rotates one curated quote per calendar day. Same quote
 * shown all day, fresh tomorrow. Date-seeded client-side so it works
 * with the static build.
 *
 * Allocation = a seeded shuffle-bag: every quote appears exactly once
 * before any repeats, the order reshuffles each full pass through the
 * list, and authors are de-clustered so the same voice never lands two
 * days running. Deterministic per-cycle, so all visitors see the same
 * quote on the same day. See the script block for details.
 *
 * Curated from the user's list: Kakashi-inspired originals, Itachi,
 * Ayanokoji-inspired originals,
 * anime/anonymous lines, Diggy originals, Luke Belmar, Greg Plitt,
 * Bill Beswick, Tate, Saint (Snowfall), Mudano (Tougen Anki), and
 * Naofumi-inspired originals (The Rising of the Shield Hero), and
 * other source-checked/original lines. Inspired entries are labeled as
 * original writing in the data below rather than presented as canon quotes.
 */

const quotes = [
  // ── Kakashi-inspired originals (user-selected) ────────────
  {
    text: "You can carry the past without letting it choose your next move.",
    author: 'Kakashi-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "Being late is forgivable. Arriving without a plan is not.",
    author: 'Kakashi-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },

  // ── Itachi Uchiha (Naruto) ────────────────────────────────
  {
    text: "True shinobi do not seek glory. They protect from the shadows.",
    author: 'Itachi Uchiha',
    source: 'Naruto',
  },
  {
    text: "You do not need forgiveness to finish what you started.",
    author: 'Itachi-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },

  // ── Ayanokoji ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  {
    text: "The greater the ability, the humbler the person. The lower it is, the more arrogant he is.",
    author: 'Ayanokoji Kiyotaka',
    source: 'Classroom of the Elite',
  },
  {
    text: "All people are nothing but tools. It doesn't matter how it's done. It doesn't matter what needs to be sacrificed. In this world, winning is everything.",
    author: 'Ayanokoji Kiyotaka',
    source: 'Classroom of the Elite',
  },
  {
    text: "People who can't do it are the ones who decide that they can't do it.",
    author: 'Ayanokoji Kiyotaka',
    source: 'Classroom of the Elite',
  },
  {
    text: "Winning is useful. Understanding why you won is better.",
    author: 'Ayanokoji-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "Are human beings truly equal?",
    author: 'Ayanokoji Kiyotaka',
    source: 'Classroom of the Elite',
  },

  // ── Mudano (Tougen Anki) ──────────────────────────────────
  {
    text: "Do not die for your goal. Live through it for your goal.",
    author: 'Mudano',
    source: 'Tougen Anki',
  },
  {
    text: "You are not allowed to call it fate before you test your strength.",
    author: 'Mudano-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },

  // ── Naofumi-inspired originals (user-selected) ────────────
  {
    text: "They can doubt me. The work still has to get done.",
    author: 'Naofumi-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "I stopped waiting for fairness and started building leverage.",
    author: 'Naofumi-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },

  // ── Diggy originals ───────────────────────────────────────
  {
    text: "Everyone plays not to lose. You have to play to dominate.",
    author: 'Diggy',
    source: 'maxxtopia',
  },

  // ── Anime / anonymous lines from the brief ────────────────
  {
    text: "Show me results and I'll overlook your failure. If you're not a prodigy amongst prodigies, you're just wasting my time.",
    author: 'unknown',
  },
  {
    text: "See the enemy you should respect — not the enemy you despise.",
    author: 'unknown',
  },
  {
    text: "But don't the mediocre surpass naturals in the end?",
    author: 'unknown',
  },
  {
    text: "You talk a big game, but I know you don't wanna give up. Most people would've tossed it. You're still holding on.",
    author: 'unknown',
  },
  {
    text: "You can't know your strength until you know your weakness. Do with that what you will. Maybe I'll see you around. I would love to see you prove my point.",
    author: 'unknown',
  },
  {
    text: "If it ends here, that just means this is how far I was meant to go.",
    author: 'unknown',
  },
  {
    text: "I don't care if I win. I want to go to war.",
    author: 'unknown',
  },

  // ── Luke Belmar ────────────────────────────────────────────
  {
    text: "Be obsessed with the path you've chosen. Not the outcome.",
    author: 'Luke Belmar',
  },
  {
    text: "Take massive action. The market doesn't care about your feelings.",
    author: 'Luke Belmar',
  },
  {
    text: "Create the delusion of abundance — that is, if it's even possible.",
    author: 'Luke Belmar',
  },

  // ── Greg Plitt ─────────────────────────────────────────────
  {
    text: "Set the standard high. Then exceed it.",
    author: 'Greg Plitt',
  },
  {
    text: "Don't be the average person doing the average thing.",
    author: 'Greg Plitt',
  },
  {
    text: "You should only be nervous if you didn't put in the time. If you've done everything in your power to prepare for this moment, there's nothing to be nervous about.",
    author: 'Greg Plitt',
  },

  // ── Bill Beswick ───────────────────────────────────────────
  {
    text: "How you think determines how you feel. How you feel determines how you act. How you act determines what happens.",
    author: 'Bill Beswick',
  },
  {
    text: "Your thoughts set the direction. Your habits decide the distance.",
    author: 'Bill Beswick-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "Control the controllables. Let go of the rest.",
    author: 'Bill Beswick',
  },
  {
    text: "You cannot command the result, but you can command the next action.",
    author: 'Bill Beswick-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "It's about maximizing yourself.",
    author: 'Bill Beswick',
  },

  // ── A.T. ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  {
    text: "Stress is the gym for the mind.",
    author: 'Tate',
  },
  {
    text: "Comfort asks you to wait. Ambition asks you to decide.",
    author: 'Tate-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "If you need everyone to approve the plan, you are not leading it.",
    author: 'Tate-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "Strength is choosing the hard thing without needing applause.",
    author: 'Tate-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "Pressure does not create your character. It removes the excuses covering it.",
    author: 'Tate-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "My unmatched perspicacity, coupled with sheer indefatigability, makes me a feared opponent in every realm of human endeavor.",
    author: 'Tate',
  },

  // ── Franklin Saint (Snowfall) ──────────────────────────────
  {
    text: "Know what I learned? The game is rigged. It ain't made for people like us — so you know what? I'm rewriting the rules.",
    author: 'Saint',
    source: 'Snowfall',
  },
  {
    text: "I built this shit. Brick by brick.",
    author: 'Saint',
    source: 'Snowfall',
  },
  {
    text: "You do not inherit leverage. You build it.",
    author: 'Saint-inspired',
    source: 'Original writing',
  },
  {
    text: "Y'all go out on your own? Fine. But don't for one second fuck around with what I gotta do to get mine — cause I promise you, there's nothing I'm not prepared to do.",
    author: 'Saint',
    source: 'Snowfall',
  },
  {
    text: "I tried to do shit the right way. Went to the other side.",
    author: 'Saint',
    source: 'Snowfall',
  },
];
---

<aside class="daily-quote" id="daily-quote" aria-label="Quote of the day">
  <!-- Hidden seed list — JS picks one based on the day. -->
  <ul class="daily-quote__source" hidden>
    {quotes.map((q) => (
      <li
        data-text={q.text}
        data-author={q.author}
        data-source={q.source ?? ''}
      ></li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <!-- Collapsed pill — visible when widget is minimized. -->
  <button
    type="button"
    class="daily-quote__pill"
    id="daily-quote-pill"
    aria-label="Show quote of the day"
    aria-expanded="false"
    hidden
  >
    <span class="daily-quote__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="daily-quote__pill-label">QOTD</span>
  </button>

  <!-- Expanded card -->
  <div class="daily-quote__card" id="daily-quote-card">
    <div class="daily-quote__topbar">
      <p class="daily-quote__eyebrow">
        <span class="daily-quote__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        QUOTE OF THE DAY
      </p>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="daily-quote__close"
        id="daily-quote-close"
        aria-label="Minimize quote of the day"
      >
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M5 12h14"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="daily-quote__text" data-quote-text>
      {quotes[0].text}
    </blockquote>
    <footer class="daily-quote__cite">
      <span class="daily-quote__author" data-quote-author>{quotes[0].author}</span>
      <span class="daily-quote__source-name" data-quote-source>{quotes[0].source ?? ''}</span>
    </footer>
  </div>
</aside>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    const root = document.getElementById('daily-quote');
    if (!root) return;
    const items = root.querySelectorAll('.daily-quote__source li');
    if (items.length === 0) return;

    // ── Shuffle-bag allocation ───────────────────────────────────
    // Goal: every quote shows exactly once before any repeats (even
    // coverage), the order reshuffles each full pass so it never feels
    // mechanical, and it's deterministic per-cycle so every visitor
    // sees the same quote on the same calendar day (required: this is
    // a static build, no server to coordinate). Same quote all day,
    // rotates at midnight.
    const N = items.length;
    const day = Math.floor(Date.now() / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));
    const cycle  = Math.floor(day / N); // which pass through the arsenal
    const within = day % N;             // position inside this pass

    // Deterministic PRNG (mulberry32), seeded by the cycle number so the
    // whole pass is stable but each new pass gets a fresh shuffle.
    const mulberry32 = (seed) => () => {
      seed |= 0; seed = (seed + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;
      let t = Math.imul(seed ^ (seed >>> 15), 1 | seed);
      t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;
      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;
    };
    const rand = mulberry32((cycle + 1) * 2654435761);

    // Fisher–Yates shuffle of the index bag.
    const order = Array.from(items, (li, i) => ({
      i,
      author: li.getAttribute('data-author') || '',
    }));
    for (let k = order.length - 1; k > 0; k--) {
      const j = Math.floor(rand() * (k + 1));
      const tmp = order[k]; order[k] = order[j]; order[j] = tmp;
    }

    // De-cluster authors: pull a different-author quote forward whenever
    // two of the same voice would land on back-to-back days.
    for (let k = 1; k < order.length; k++) {
      if (order[k].author && order[k].author === order[k - 1].author) {
        for (let m = k + 1; m < order.length; m++) {
          if (order[m].author !== order[k - 1].author) {
            const tmp = order[k]; order[k] = order[m]; order[m] = tmp;
            break;
          }
        }
      }
    }

    const idx  = order[within].i;
    const pick = items[idx];

    const text   = pick.getAttribute('data-text')   || '';
    const author = pick.getAttribute('data-author') || '';
    const source = pick.getAttribute('data-source') || '';

    const $text   = root.querySelector('[data-quote-text]');
    const $author = root.querySelector('[data-quote-author]');
    const $source = root.querySelector('[data-quote-source]');

    if ($text)   $text.textContent   = text;
    if ($author) $author.textContent = author;
    if ($source) $source.textContent = source;
    if ($source && !source) $source.style.display = 'none';

    // ── Auto-fit ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Longer quotes scale their font down a notch so they always sit
    // cleanly inside the fixed-width card — no cramping, no overflow,
    // no clipped lines. Length-based tiers (cheap + deterministic,
    // works the same for every visitor on the static build). The base
    // size lives in CSS per breakpoint; this only sets the multiplier.
    const len = text.length;
    const scale = len <= 90 ? 1 : len <= 150 ? 0.92 : len <= 210 ? 0.82 : 0.74;
    root.style.setProperty('--qotd-scale', String(scale));

    // ── Collapse / expand ────────────────────────────────────────
    const STORAGE_KEY = 'maxxtopia_qotd_collapsed';
    const card  = document.getElementById('daily-quote-card');
    const pill  = document.getElementById('daily-quote-pill');
    const close = document.getElementById('daily-quote-close');
    if (!card || !pill || !close) return;

    const setCollapsed = (collapsed) => {
      if (collapsed) {
        card.setAttribute('hidden', '');
        pill.removeAttribute('hidden');
        pill.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      } else {
        card.removeAttribute('hidden');
        pill.setAttribute('hidden', '');
        pill.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
      }
      sessionStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, collapsed ? '1' : '0');
    };

    // Phones keep their existing collapse/expand behavior. Desktop opens the
    // card on every visit so the quote is visible without requiring a click;
    // the mobile preference remains session-persistent.
    const storedCollapsed = sessionStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
    const isMobile = window.matchMedia('(max-width: 768px)').matches;
    const startCollapsed = isMobile && storedCollapsed === '1';
    setCollapsed(startCollapsed);

    close.addEventListener('click', () => setCollapsed(true));
    pill.addEventListener('click',  () => setCollapsed(false));

    // ── Auto-minimize after 5 minutes on the site ────────────────
    // Once a visitor has been on the page ~5 min, tuck the card down to
    // the pill so it stops taking up the corner during a long read/scroll.
    // Fires once; if they re-open it afterward it stays open (we don't nag).
    const AUTO_MINIMIZE_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000;
    setTimeout(() => {
      if (!card.hasAttribute('hidden')) setCollapsed(true);
    }, AUTO_MINIMIZE_MS);

    // ── Auto-minimize on game interaction ────────────────────────
    // On the /play page the Sprite Cannon game is embedded as an iframe
    // (#sc-frame). The moment the player clicks/taps into it, collapse the
    // widget so the card never sits over the run. Interacting with an iframe
    // blurs the parent window and makes the iframe the activeElement — that's
    // our cross-frame signal (the game's own events don't bubble out). We only
    // minimize; we never fight the player by re-opening it.
    const gameFrame = document.getElementById('sc-frame');
    if (gameFrame) {
      window.addEventListener('blur', () => {
        // Defer a tick so activeElement has settled to the iframe.
        setTimeout(() => {
          if (document.activeElement === gameFrame && !card.hasAttribute('hidden')) {
            setCollapsed(true);
          }
        }, 0);
      });
    }

    // ── Idle fade ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // After 60s without hover, the widget fades to ~25% opacity.
    // Hovering anywhere on it cancels the fade; mouseleave restarts
    // the timer. Applies to both card and pill states.
    const FADE_AFTER_MS = 60_000;
    let fadeTimer = null;

    const armFade = () => {
      if (fadeTimer) clearTimeout(fadeTimer);
      fadeTimer = setTimeout(() => {
        root.classList.add('is-faded');
      }, FADE_AFTER_MS);
    };
    const wakeUp = () => {
      if (fadeTimer) clearTimeout(fadeTimer);
      root.classList.remove('is-faded');
    };

    root.addEventListener('mouseenter', wakeUp);
    root.addEventListener('focusin',    wakeUp);
    root.addEventListener('mouseleave', armFade);
    root.addEventListener('focusout',   armFade);

    // Also wake up + re-arm when expand/collapse happens, so the
    // newly-visible state gets a fresh 60s window before fading.
    [pill, close].forEach((el) =>
      el.addEventListener('click', () => { wakeUp(); armFade(); })
    );

    armFade();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  /* ── Floating QOTD widget ─────────────────────────────────────────
     Fixed bottom-right, always visible across every page during
     scroll. Collapses to a small "QOTD" pill via the close button;
     pill expands back to the card on click. State persists in
     sessionStorage. ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .daily-quote {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 20px;
    right: 20px;
    z-index: 50;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 700ms cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0.5, 1);
  }
  .daily-quote > * { pointer-events: auto; }
  /* Idle fade — kicks in 60s after last hover/focus.
     Wakes back up to 1 instantly on mouseenter (no transition delay
     on the wake-up; the transition above only runs on the fade-out).
     Faded state stays clickable: pill is still visible enough to find,
     and hovering it brings the card right back. */
  .daily-quote.is-faded { opacity: 0.22; }
  .daily-quote.is-faded:hover,
  .daily-quote.is-faded:focus-within { opacity: 1; }

  /* Pill (collapsed state) */
  .daily-quote__pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 30% 30%, rgba(226, 91, 255, 0.22), transparent 60%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(20, 12, 36, 0.92), rgba(10, 6, 18, 0.96));
    border: 1px solid rgba(226, 91, 255, 0.55);
    color: #fbe7ff;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04),
      0 14px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5),
      0 0 24px rgba(226, 91, 255, 0.25);
    transition: transform 200ms ease, box-shadow 200ms ease, border-color 200ms ease;
  }
  .daily-quote__pill:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: #e25bff;
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06),
      0 18px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55),
      0 0 32px rgba(226, 91, 255, 0.45);
  }
  .daily-quote__pill-label {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .daily-quote__pill[hidden] { display: none !important; }

  /* Card (expanded state) */
  .daily-quote__card {
    position: relative;
    width: min(360px, calc(100vw - 40px));
    padding: 16px 18px 18px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong);
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 0% 0%, rgba(226, 91, 255, 0.14), transparent 55%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 100% 100%, rgba(76, 81, 247, 0.14), transparent 55%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(20, 12, 36, 0.94), rgba(10, 6, 18, 0.97));
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05),
      0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55),
      0 0 40px rgba(226, 91, 255, 0.10);
    overflow: hidden;
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    animation: qotd-card-in 240ms ease-out;
  }
  .daily-quote__card[hidden] { display: none !important; }
  @keyframes qotd-card-in {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px) scale(0.96); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0)   scale(1); }
  }
  /* Magenta accent edge on the left — quote-block bar */
  .daily-quote__card::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0; top: 12px; bottom: 12px;
    width: 3px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #e25bff 0%, #4c51f7 60%, #00d4ff 100%);
    box-shadow: 0 0 14px rgba(226, 91, 255, 0.5);
  }

  /* Top bar — eyebrow + close */
  .daily-quote__topbar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .daily-quote__close {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 160ms ease, border-color 160ms ease, color 160ms ease;
  }
  .daily-quote__close:hover {
    background: rgba(226, 91, 255, 0.14);
    border-color: rgba(226, 91, 255, 0.55);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Eyebrow */
  .daily-quote__eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-cyan);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .daily-quote__dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: #e25bff;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px #e25bff;
    animation: quote-dot 2s ease-in-out infinite;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  @keyframes quote-dot {
    0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
    50%      { opacity: 0.6; transform: scale(0.85); }
  }

  /* Quote text — Crimson Pro italic. Classical-modern book serif used
     across high-end editorial publishing. Reads like a printed
     pull-quote with proper italic ligatures, no comic-book energy. */
  .daily-quote__text {
    font-family: 'Crimson Pro', 'Georgia', 'Times New Roman', serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: calc(16.5px * var(--qotd-scale, 1));
    line-height: 1.32;
    letter-spacing: -0.003em;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 10px;
    /* pretty, not balance: balance equalizes line widths (good for short
       headings) but strands lines on longer quotes, giving an uneven "off"
       rag. pretty keeps a natural rag + kills orphans at every length. */
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .daily-quote__text::before { content: '“'; opacity: 0.7; margin-right: 3px; color: var(--color-magenta); font-weight: 600; }
  .daily-quote__text::after  { content: '”'; opacity: 0.7; margin-left: 3px;  color: var(--color-cyan);    font-weight: 600; }

  /* Citation */
  .daily-quote__cite {
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding-left: 10px;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .daily-quote__author::before { content: '— '; color: var(--color-subtle); }
  .daily-quote__author {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .daily-quote__source-name {
    color: var(--color-subtle);
  }
  .daily-quote__source-name:not(:empty)::before { content: '· '; }

  /* Mobile — keep it visible but tuck slightly out of the way */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .daily-quote {
      bottom: 14px;
      right: 14px;
    }
    .daily-quote__card {
      width: min(300px, calc(100vw - 28px));
      padding: 14px 14px 16px;
    }
    .daily-quote__text { font-size: calc(13.5px * var(--qotd-scale, 1)); }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .daily-quote__dot,
    .daily-quote__card { animation: none !important; }
  }
</style>
